{
 "manufacturer": "Woodward",
 "manufacturer_slug": "woodward",
 "model": "MSLC-2 Master Synchronizer and Load Control",
 "model_slug": "mslc-2",
 "short_model": "MSLC-2",
 "aliases": [
  "MSLC2",
  "MSLC-2 master synchronizer"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Generator controller (utility-tie master synchronizer)",
 "applies_to": "MSLC-2, data protocol 5200, per manual 37444G.",
 "summary": "The MSLC-2 sits at the utility tie or bus breaker of a DSLC-2 generator plant: it synchronises the plant bus to the utility and runs import/export, base-load and process control for the DSLC-2 units. It is a Modbus RTU slave on RS-485 and a Modbus/TCP slave on Ethernet. Measurements and states come from data protocol 5200 at Modicon 450001; interface setpoints and remote discrete-input commands are parameters. This map covers system A/B frequencies and phase angle, 32-bit system A power, voltage and current, energy, control modes, flags, alarms, relays and inputs.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU",
  "TCP"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baud": 19200,
  "parity": "None",
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "0-based",
  "note": "The 5200 table prints both the bus address (50000) and the Modicon address (450001); this map records and sends the bus address. Parameters use Modicon 40000 + (parameter ID + 1), so parameter 7642 is Modicon 47643 = wire address 7642. The manual's ModScan32 screenshot for parameter 7642 uses address 7643 (1-based), which confirms this; its worked example prints '407642', a typo that does not follow the rule."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "MSLC-2 Master Synchronizer and Load Control - Manual",
  "doc_number": "37444G",
  "revision_date": "2022-02-09",
  "url": "https://www.woodward.com/products/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2024/08/37444_G.pdf",
  "pages": "pp. 180-186 (Modbus address range, visualization, parameter rule, interface setpoints, discrete inputs over interface, loss of connection), p. 194 (Modbus parameters), pp. 201-210 (data protocol 5200), serial interface parameters in the configuration chapter"
 },
 "notes": [
  "The 5200 table states size (16/32 bit) and format (signed / bit array) for each value. The shared DSLC-2/MSLC-2 Modbus chapter says 32-bit values are sent high word at the lower address, so 32-bit values are ABCD.",
  "System A is the utility / mains side and system B the plant bus side as used throughout the MSLC-2 manual.",
  "Left out: the 16-bit power, voltage and current values at 50011-50031 (scaled by exponent registers 50001-50003; use the 32-bit block from 50100), values with only a range instead of a multiplier (AI4-AI6, process and PF references, ASA/CBS numbers) and unnamed bits.",
  "Load and reactive load control mode enums are printed for both MSLC-2 and DSLC-2; only the MSLC-2 meanings are listed here.",
  "Interface setpoints need no password but only take effect when their setpoint-source parameter (7634, 7635, 7783, 7784) is set to Interface.",
  "Bits of 7644/7645 in manual order 01-16: Check, Permissive, Run, CB Aux, Voltage raise, Voltage lower, Base load, Utility unload, Ramp pause, Setpoint raise, Setpoint lower, Process, Imp./Exp. control, Modbus reset, System update, N/A. The manual does not say whether bit 01 is the least significant bit."
 ],
